  "slug": "sequences-promoter-38cf",
  "summary": "AlphaFold 3 accuracy drops on novel RNAs, driving validation and confidence scoring for RNA and protein-RNA predictions.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is assessing when deep-learning structure predictions for RNA and RNA-containing complexes can be trusted against experimental references. An AlphaFold 3 evaluation across more than 1,300 protein-RNA complexes and about 270 RNA-only systems reports that fold and interface accuracy decline for novel RNAs. On the validation side, conkit-validate is extended to RNA as a mapless method that compares predicted contact patterns with deposited structures, while the ipSAE score is generalized with directional PAE scoring to protein, nucleic acid, ligand and ion interactions in AF3 and Boltz-2 cofolding models. Ribocentre-FoldBridge links RNA chemical probing data to 3D structures. CryoID2 applies a 3D U-Net to cryoEM maps to identify protein and RNA candidates, a related but distinct task. The emphasis is on generalization and reliability rather than on model generation alone.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-09"
}
